---
title: "rls_policy_members (0000_create_member_schema)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_role: evaluate request role
    q_check_role --> q_service_all: role = service_role
    q_check_role --> q_auth_check: role = authenticated
    q_check_role --> q_deny: role = anon or other

    q_service_all --> q_allow: USING(true) WITH CHECK(true) -- all operations
    q_auth_check --> q_check_op: check operation type
    q_check_op --> q_allow_read: operation = SELECT -- USING(true)
    q_check_op --> q_check_owner: operation = UPDATE -- USING(auth.uid() = id)
    q_check_op --> q_deny: operation = INSERT or DELETE

    q_check_owner --> q_allow: auth.uid() = id (own row only)
    q_check_owner --> q_deny: auth.uid() != id

    q_allow_read --> q_allow: return rows
    q_allow --> [*]: access granted
    q_deny --> [*]: access denied

    note right of q_check_role
        INV-001: service_role has unrestricted access to all operations
        INV-002: authenticated users can SELECT all rows
        INV-003: authenticated users can UPDATE only their own row (auth.uid() = id)
        INV-004: authenticated users CANNOT INSERT or DELETE member rows
        INV-005: anon role has NO access (no policy grants access)
    end note

    note right of q_check_owner
        INV-006: Self-update check uses auth.uid() = id (Supabase JWT uid matches PK)
        INV-007: No WITH CHECK on update policy -- user could set is_admin = TRUE on own row
    end note
